  "sc:description": "FruitDBase was conceived to address a gap in the bioinformatics landscape: the lack of a species-centric, quality-controlled transcriptomic resource for Prunus dulcis (almond). While general-purpose repositories such as NCBI SRA, ENA, and GDR provide valuable raw and genomic data, they lack the curation and integration needed for efficient comparative studies.\n\nThe project currently provides a curated expression atlas for P. dulcis, based on uniformly processed RNA-seq data and supported by interactive exploration tools. For other Prunus species, FruitDBase offers access to available public SRA datasets, laying the groundwork for future atlas development across the genus.",
  "sc:funder": "Momentum CSIC Programme: Develop Your Digital Talent (European Commission – NextGenerationEU)",
  "sc:isAccessibleForFree": true,
  "sc:license": "GPL-3.0",
  "sc:name": "FruitDBase",
